WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.150
- These kids back here have no
idea what's about to happen.

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:05.700
I'm about to give them a
hundred dollars in cash,

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:07.150
one hour to spend it.

00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:10.050
If they don't spend it in an
hour they don't get anything.

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:11.030
Let's go surprise 'em.

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:11.863
Come on.

00:00:11.863 --> 00:00:12.700
I have a challenge for you.

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:13.840
You think you're up to it?

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:14.673
- Yeah.

00:00:14.673 --> 00:00:15.506
- What is that?

00:00:15.506 --> 00:00:16.339
- Money.

00:00:16.339 --> 00:00:17.172
- A hundred dollars.

00:00:17.219 --> 00:00:18.851
(laughing)

00:00:18.851 --> 00:00:19.851
- A hundred.

00:00:21.061 --> 00:00:23.311
(laughing)

00:00:23.973 --> 00:00:24.806
No.

00:00:24.806 --> 00:00:28.020
- You have one hour to
spend a hundred dollars.

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:29.603
- I got an hour?

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:32.500
- If you don't spend all
the money in the hour

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:34.360
you don't get to keep anything you bought.

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:35.595
What do you think you're going to do,

00:00:35.595 --> 00:00:36.450
what's your plan of attack?

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:37.763
- Maybe give it to people?

00:00:38.309 --> 00:00:39.142
- Candy.

00:00:39.142 --> 00:00:39.975
- Ice cream.

00:00:39.975 --> 00:00:41.010
- Let's go, let's find that ice cream.

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:41.843
What are you going to get?

00:00:41.843 --> 00:00:43.860
- Stuff for my room and stuff for school.

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:45.370
- [Host] Where do you wanna go,
you have to make a decision.

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:46.203
- Dylan's Candy Bar.

00:00:46.203 --> 00:00:47.530
- All right, you're
going to Candy Bar first?

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:49.860
Ready, the timer starts now.

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:50.693
Let's go.

00:00:50.693 --> 00:00:51.530
- You got to run.

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:55.373
There's this toy called Treasure X.

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:58.333
It comes with this little skeleton guy.

00:00:58.630 --> 00:01:00.740
- [Host] You have to be able
to spend it all in an hour.

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:01.623
- All of it?

00:01:01.630 --> 00:01:02.463
- All of it.

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:04.803
- I don't know.

00:01:04.810 --> 00:01:06.570
- [Host] I see an ice cream truck guys.

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:08.683
- [Sal] Let's get it before it goes away.

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:10.350
- [Annie] Finally, we made it.

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:11.350
- [Host] We made it.

00:01:13.106 --> 00:01:14.606
- [Annie] Vanilla.

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:17.183
- [Host] Okay.

00:01:17.183 --> 00:01:18.016
- One hundred.

00:01:19.870 --> 00:01:22.163
- Here, put it in here
and then hold on to it.

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:26.140
- We'll go to the toy store first.

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:28.153
Oh be careful.

00:01:40.072 --> 00:01:42.060
- [Sal] Can I just eat my ice cream now?

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:44.450
- [Host] Yeah, but just so
you know time is ticking.

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:46.210
You're gonna have 40 minutes
left to spend the money.

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:47.580
You only spent four of the dollars.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:48.980
What are you gonna get Owen?

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:51.027
- I'm looking for it.

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:52.940
That's Minecraft.

00:01:52.940 --> 00:01:53.773
- [Host] You like that?

00:01:53.773 --> 00:01:54.910
- That's a little TNT mug.

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:58.503
Look at it, it's a hilarious mug.

00:01:58.748 --> 00:01:59.910
$9.99.

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:01.253
- [Host] What are you looking for again?

00:02:01.253 --> 00:02:05.803
- It's like a piece of gold
and a weird skeleton figure.

00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:08.700
I have no idea if it's even here.

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:10.950
- Let's see, is there
anything else you want?

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:11.983
- Not really.

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:14.800
- If I were a kid I'd be
grabbing everything I see.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:16.203
Owen's very particular.

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:17.800
He really wants this one toy.

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:20.433
- How many minutes was it already?

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:22.683
At least I got some change back.

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:24.460
- There's Dylan's Candy Bar.

00:02:25.779 --> 00:02:26.946
- [Skyla] Wow.

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:29.520
- [Host] Anything seem good, that?

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:31.833
You gonna get stuff
here, what do you like?

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:37.383
You're getting a lot of different stuff.

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:41.740
- Come on Sal, don't be
scared of a brain freeze,

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:43.280
you gonna eat so fast right,

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:45.229
'cause we gotta get to spend that money.

00:02:45.229 --> 00:02:46.062
(giggling)

00:02:46.062 --> 00:02:48.040
What are you going to
do with your money now?

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:50.040
- [Sal] I'm going to put it in the bank.

00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:51.350
- That's, you don't want to get toys,

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:52.630
you want to put it in the bank?

00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:54.403
- [Sal] Let's do this money thing!

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:55.883
Are those pigeons?

00:02:55.910 --> 00:02:57.760
- Yeah, there are a bunch of pigeons.

00:02:58.140 --> 00:02:59.690
- [Annie] There's a lot of pigeons.

00:02:59.690 --> 00:03:01.540
- [Host] Come on, don't get distracted.

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:02.373
All right, so we're going to walk

00:03:02.373 --> 00:03:03.570
through the farmer's market.

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:04.830
- [Sal] I'm getting corn.

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:06.543
- It says five for two dollars.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:10.703
- It's because I don't
want to eat too much corn.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.030
- [Host] Yeah, do you have a plan?

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:17.203
- I don't know, maybe flowers.

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:18.510
- These ones.

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:19.860
- [Host] You want this one?

00:03:20.077 --> 00:03:21.270
- Come on spend this money.

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:22.583
I'm buying it for someone.

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:24.070
- Oh, you're buying it for someone?

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:24.903
- Yep.

00:03:24.903 --> 00:03:25.736
- That's nice of you.

00:03:26.410 --> 00:03:27.243
It's for me?

00:03:29.302 --> 00:03:30.873
Oh my god that's so sweet.

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:32.910
- [Sal] Is it four dollars?

00:03:35.874 --> 00:03:36.707
- Two.

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:38.943
- [Sal] We're really spending this money.

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:50.860
- You're gonna have to
pay for the cab though.

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:51.763
- [Owen] Yes.

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:54.230
- You're willing to do
it to get to that toy?

00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:55.063
- [Owen] Yeah.

00:03:55.648 --> 00:03:57.011
- [Host] All right, let's
do it, let's hail a cab.

00:03:57.011 --> 00:03:57.844
- Cab!

00:03:58.793 --> 00:03:59.626
Hi!

00:03:59.626 --> 00:04:01.873
- [Host] How much do you think
you're gonna spend at Target?

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:05.890
You know what I think we should see

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:07.370
how much all this stuff is

00:04:07.670 --> 00:04:09.820
to make sure you can
get it all, all right?

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:14.443
- Whatever candy I like I
got and some random stuff.

00:04:14.930 --> 00:04:16.743
I want cotton candy please.

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:18.500
- [Host] You know how
cotton candy gets made?

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:19.333
- With sugar.

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:21.460
My brothers, they're gonna be jealous.

00:04:21.473 --> 00:04:23.723
(laughing)

00:04:23.813 --> 00:04:24.646
- Here you go.

00:04:24.713 --> 00:04:25.713
- Thank you.

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:28.693
- I'm going to be the
coolest kid in school.

00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:31.763
- This is kind of like
the craziest contest.

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:35.323
I'm going to pay you by dollars.

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:37.473
How much money is it?

00:04:37.633 --> 00:04:38.863
- [Cab Driver] $9.90.

00:04:38.863 --> 00:04:40.343
- Nine, 10.

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:45.073
Here I'll give you four
or five dollars for it.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:45.923
- [Host] Yeah, save some.

00:04:45.923 --> 00:04:48.053
- All right I'll give you a little more.

00:04:48.310 --> 00:04:50.833
I know it sounds really expensive but.

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:52.803
I gave a lot of money away.

00:04:55.490 --> 00:04:57.320
- [Host] That's why you put
it in the bank, to save it?

00:04:57.320 --> 00:05:00.093
- Because I really don't
want to spend that money.

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:01.779
- [Host] Wait a second, Sal.

00:05:01.779 --> 00:05:02.612
- What?

00:05:02.612 --> 00:05:04.140
- Here's a bank, do you want to stop in?

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:05.810
Did you want to stop and
put your money in now?

00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:08.823
- [Sal] No, I want to go
to the toy store instead.

00:05:08.823 --> 00:05:09.656
- Okay we're going to the toy store.

00:05:09.656 --> 00:05:10.489
Tiles.

00:05:10.489 --> 00:05:12.323
- [Host] Do you guys
want to buy any tiles?

00:05:12.739 --> 00:05:14.179
- [Sal] No.
- [Annie] No.

00:05:14.179 --> 00:05:15.012
- [Host] No, okay sure.

00:05:15.211 --> 00:05:19.051
- [Sal] We're almost there.

00:05:19.051 --> 00:05:20.218
- [Host] Whew.

00:05:20.668 --> 00:05:22.001
- I'm all right.

00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:23.013
- [Host] Whew.

00:05:23.955 --> 00:05:24.928
Do you see it?

00:05:24.928 --> 00:05:25.761
- Yeah!

00:05:26.270 --> 00:05:27.883
X marks the spot.

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:30.523
- [Host] Do you want to pick
out some more stuff to get?

00:05:32.110 --> 00:05:35.707
- I might spend the rest on that one.

00:05:36.176 --> 00:05:38.031
To upstairs!

00:05:38.031 --> 00:05:38.864
All right.

00:05:40.029 --> 00:05:41.446
- [Host] Careful.

00:05:41.845 --> 00:05:44.317
- [Owen] Nice, let's take the elevator.

00:05:44.317 --> 00:05:45.333
- [Host] Okay, what do you guys want?

00:05:47.690 --> 00:05:48.523
Unicorns?

00:05:48.523 --> 00:05:49.360
What do you like?

00:05:49.817 --> 00:05:50.650
You like unicorns?

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:51.483
Should I grab one?

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:53.063
Oh okay you want that one.

00:05:53.165 --> 00:05:53.998
- [Annie] Mm-hmm.

00:05:53.998 --> 00:05:54.831
- All right good.

00:05:54.831 --> 00:05:55.800
All right, there's one thing.

00:05:55.910 --> 00:05:57.660
That's 10 bucks so you got
a lot more you can get.

00:05:57.660 --> 00:05:58.493
- I can hold that.

00:05:58.493 --> 00:06:00.340
- You only have a certain amount of time.

00:06:00.340 --> 00:06:01.173
- [Sal] Found it.

00:06:01.173 --> 00:06:02.503
- [Host] Found, that's something you want?

00:06:02.503 --> 00:06:03.883
- Ours is broken now.

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:05.410
- [Host] That's smart, that's smart.

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:06.593
Replace broken things.

00:06:07.150 --> 00:06:09.773
- I'm not getting a
costume until Halloween.

00:06:09.870 --> 00:06:12.123
- Okay, well you could
get it for Halloween.

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:14.493
- I feel like I want a costume.

00:06:15.090 --> 00:06:16.590
Hey do you want a bow and arrow?

00:06:16.590 --> 00:06:17.423
- Yeah.

00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:18.770
I want a bow and arrow.

00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:21.023
Just think think think.

00:06:21.040 --> 00:06:22.750
- We just went to Dylan's Candy Bar.

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:23.940
Where are we going next?

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:24.773
- Yeah.

00:06:24.773 --> 00:06:25.606
Ross's.

00:06:25.606 --> 00:06:27.700
- You have 10 minutes, do
you think you can do it?

00:06:28.337 --> 00:06:30.249
- [Skyla] Yeah.

00:06:30.249 --> 00:06:31.082
- Yes!

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:35.253
Wait, I'm already paying so I made it.

00:06:35.320 --> 00:06:36.510
- You might have some leftover

00:06:36.510 --> 00:06:38.950
and then you have to
get rid of that money.

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:40.090
How much money do you have left?

00:06:40.090 --> 00:06:40.923
Four dollars?

00:06:41.208 --> 00:06:42.041
- Yeah.

00:06:42.041 --> 00:06:42.874
- [Host] Okay.

00:06:42.874 --> 00:06:43.937
- One two three.

00:06:43.937 --> 00:06:45.900
- You might want to get more Annie.

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:48.150
(laughing)

00:06:48.692 --> 00:06:49.525
Annie.

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:51.733
Do you need help Annie?

00:06:52.811 --> 00:06:54.461
And then I'm going to count them.

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:56.247
Nine, 10.

00:06:57.087 --> 00:06:58.004
- [Sal] 71.

00:06:59.127 --> 00:07:00.719
- [Host] Is that how
much money you have left?

00:07:00.719 --> 00:07:01.552
Do you know?

00:07:01.552 --> 00:07:02.385
- Eh.

00:07:02.385 --> 00:07:03.630
- I have one more dollar left.

00:07:03.630 --> 00:07:05.100
- What are you going to spend it on?

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:06.663
- Something in the toy store.

00:07:08.870 --> 00:07:09.920
- [Host] Do you want me
to hold that for you?

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:10.753
So let's go.

00:07:10.753 --> 00:07:12.210
Do you know what your size is?

00:07:12.260 --> 00:07:13.093
- [Skyla] Yeah.

00:07:13.093 --> 00:07:13.926
- [Host] Okay.

00:07:14.034 --> 00:07:16.553
- [Skyla] I got headbands and tights.

00:07:17.210 --> 00:07:18.043
- [Host] Nice.

00:07:18.043 --> 00:07:20.023
- I have more money left.

00:07:20.560 --> 00:07:22.113
- [Host] How much more do you need?

00:07:23.720 --> 00:07:25.140
- I have one more left.

00:07:25.140 --> 00:07:27.600
- Yeah, give me one more dollar left.

00:07:28.015 --> 00:07:28.848
20.

00:07:28.848 --> 00:07:31.113
- [Host] And how much change?

00:07:31.113 --> 00:07:31.946
Okay.

00:07:32.663 --> 00:07:33.753
- Nothing left.

00:07:33.753 --> 00:07:34.663
- [Host] Nothing left?

00:07:34.663 --> 00:07:36.453
You need nine more cents guys.

00:07:37.521 --> 00:07:39.383
- But we don't have nine more cents.

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:41.120
- [Host] What are you guys gonna do?

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:44.020
- One minute left and
you have to have to spend

00:07:44.200 --> 00:07:46.563
four dollars and some amount of change.

00:07:46.850 --> 00:07:49.660
How do you think you're gonna do it?

00:07:52.850 --> 00:07:53.683
- I'll give it to somebody.

00:07:53.683 --> 00:07:55.443
- [Host] You'll give it to
someone, okay here we go.

00:07:55.580 --> 00:08:00.580
- Mommy, I have a quarter in my backpack.

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:02.543
We can.

00:08:02.543 --> 00:08:04.003
- [Host] Annie, you're
doing that for your brother?

00:08:04.910 --> 00:08:05.743
Wow.

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:12.233
- Four dollars.

00:08:14.128 --> 00:08:14.961
You're welcome.

00:08:15.695 --> 00:08:16.833
- [Man] Good job Owen.

00:08:16.900 --> 00:08:17.733
I won.

00:08:17.733 --> 00:08:18.566
- Good.

00:08:18.566 --> 00:08:20.430
You worked together to solve this.

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:23.023
Do you think you spent your
hundred dollars wisely?

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:25.023
- Not really.

00:08:25.210 --> 00:08:27.510
- I got a hundred dollars
and I spent it good.

00:08:27.510 --> 00:08:30.963
- What made you give that woman
the four dollars at the end?

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:33.033
- She looked nice.

00:08:33.770 --> 00:08:35.440
- What felt better, helping your brother

00:08:35.440 --> 00:08:36.863
or getting all the toys?

00:08:37.980 --> 00:08:39.213
- Helping my brother.

00:08:39.840 --> 00:08:40.813
- Working together.

00:08:41.958 --> 00:08:44.708
(pleasant music)

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:48.073
- I won the challenge.

00:08:49.829 --> 00:08:51.149
- [Host] Okay we're good.

00:08:51.149 --> 00:08:52.200
That was so cute.

00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:54.950
(pleasant music)

